codex
The constructor split removed the equality mismatch, but proving all three mutually recursive claims together is expanding instead of reusing sibling circularities efficiently; memory is still safe, but this proof shape is not converging. I’m stopping that run and will collapse the mutual induction into a single self-circular claim so the backend has one invariant to reuse.
